{"title":"V Rohith Reddy Matli, Ph.D.","markdown":{"yaml":{"title":"V Rohith Reddy Matli, Ph.D.","image":"profile.jpg","about":{"template":"trestles","links":[{"icon":"envelope","text":"Email","href":"mailto:vrrmatli@gmail.com"},{"icon":"linkedin","text":"LinkedIn","href":"https://linkedin.com/in/vmatli"},{"icon":"mortarboard-fill","text":"Google Scholar","href":"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=SHjYPf8AAAAJ&hl=en&authuser=4"},{"icon":"github","text":"Github","href":"https://github.com/YOUR_GITHUB"}]}},"headingText":"Hello! 👋","containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n\n\nI am a Data Scientist and **applied researcher** with a **Ph.D. in Geospatial Analytics**. Over the past eight years, I have built predictive models to make sense of everything from telecommunication operations to ecological system responses. \n\nMy passion lies in taking complex spatial-temporal data and turning it into clear, actionable insights. I enjoy blending foundational statistical methods, like **Bayesian inference** and **geostatistics**, with **modern AI tools** to build intelligent systems and novel frameworks that help answer tough questions. \n\nRight now, my interests are lie at the intersection of **Agentic Workflows** and **Complex Spatial Networks**. I am leveraging my background in computational statistics to explore how we can design AI systems capable of reasoning through and optimizing spatial data autonomously.\n\n### Core Competencies\n* **Modelling & Statistics:** Geostatistics, Bayesian Inference, Uplift Modeling, Survival Analysis, XGBoost, Generalized Additive Models (GAMs), Monte Carlo Simulation.\n* **Programming & Data:** Python, R, SQL, SAS, Matlab, Amazon Redshift, PostgreSQL.\n* **BI & Geospatial:** Tableau, Power BI, ArcGIS/QGIS, Alteryx.\n* **AI Integration:** Prompt Engineering, GenAI integrations, Agentic Workflows (In Progress).\n\n\n*This website is a portfolio of my experiments with agentic workflows and anything I find interesting in general.*\n","srcMarkdownNoYaml":"\n\n## Hello! 👋\n\nI am a Data Scientist and **applied researcher** with a **Ph.D. in Geospatial Analytics**. Over the past eight years, I have built predictive models to make sense of everything from telecommunication operations to ecological system responses. \n\nMy passion lies in taking complex spatial-temporal data and turning it into clear, actionable insights. I enjoy blending foundational statistical methods, like **Bayesian inference** and **geostatistics**, with **modern AI tools** to build intelligent systems and novel frameworks that help answer tough questions. \n\nRight now, my interests are lie at the intersection of **Agentic Workflows** and **Complex Spatial Networks**. I am leveraging my background in computational statistics to explore how we can design AI systems capable of reasoning through and optimizing spatial data autonomously.\n\n### Core Competencies\n* **Modelling & Statistics:** Geostatistics, Bayesian Inference, Uplift Modeling, Survival Analysis, XGBoost, Generalized Additive Models (GAMs), Monte Carlo Simulation.\n* **Programming & Data:** Python, R, SQL, SAS, Matlab, Amazon Redshift, PostgreSQL.\n* **BI & Geospatial:** Tableau, Power BI, ArcGIS/QGIS, Alteryx.\n* **AI Integration:** Prompt Engineering, GenAI integrations, Agentic Workflows (In Progress).\n\n\n*This website is a portfolio of my experiments with agentic workflows and anything I find interesting in general.*\n"},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":null,"freeze":false,"echo":true,"output":true,"warning":true,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"engine":"markdown"},"render":{"keep-tex":false,"keep-typ":f